:"APA. The 63 in circulation was superseded in January 2026","kind":"SAYS"}],"precip":[{"n":"Bragança annual normal","claim":"774 mm","actual":"772.7 mm (1981–2010)","verdict":"CONFIRMED"},{"n":"Viana do Castelo annual normal","claim":"1,192 mm","actual":"1,470.2 mm (1971–2000)","verdict":"REFUTED"},{"n":"National precipitation, −15–20% over 20 years","claim":"−15–20%","actual":"not found in any IPMA or APA document","verdict":"NOT FOUND"},{"n":"Algarve, −30–35% over 10 years, up to −45%","claim":"−30–45%","actual":"not found; SNIRH returned 403 so the probe is incomplete","verdict":"NOT FOUND"},{"n":"Six of the ten driest years fall after 2000","claim":"6 of 10","actual":"IPMA ranks seasons, not an annual top-ten list","verdict":"NOT FOUND AS STATED"},{"n":"South precipitation, 2071–2100 vs 1971–2000","claim":"−15 to −30%","actual":"RNA2100: −15% RCP4.5, −35% RCP8.5, from 45 EURO-CORDEX runs","verdict":"PARTLY CONFIRMED, CEILING EXCEEDED"}]},"autonomy":{"spain_storage":[["Tejo / Tajo",11056,51],["Guadiana",9543,40],["Douro / Duero",7602,35],["Minho / Miño-Sil",3030,29]],"pt_shared":{"Tejo / Tajo":2855.822,"Guadiana":5231.693,"Douro / Duero":2978.58,"Minho / Miño-Sil":394.73},"spain_demand":[["Duero",3644.19,3345.58,2021],["Tejo / Tajo",3522.26,1992.55,2022],["Guadiana",2022.56,1720.55,2021]],"guad_ratio_lo":12.1,"guad_ratio_hi":15.9,"es_guadiana_cap":9543},"nulls":[["SNIRH — the national water information system","dark","HTTP 403 to every client since 29 March 2026. Verified by curl, WebFetch, proxy services and a logged-in Chrome browser on a residential IP. Wayback dates the last 200 to 6 March 2026. Untested: a Portuguese domestic IP.","snirh.apambiente.pt"],["Useful storage capacity, nationally","not published","Neither the APA weekly bulletin nor any of the eight PGRH regional inventories carries a “capacidade útil” column. Confirmed by grep against a working control.","APA / PGRH"],["Minho mainstem flow into Portugal","not measured","No active Portuguese gauge on the Minho mainstem was identified. Every Minho-basin entry in the SNIRH register — Mazedo, Foz do Mouro, Segude, Casais, Messegães — is on a tributary. Verification rests on Spain's own Frieira dam data.","SNIRH station register"],["Guadiana flow at Pomarão","estimated, not measured","The station is ATIVA, but daily values are estimated from Pulo do Lobo upstream. The 2024/25 CADC annual report states only that the daily mean stayed above 2 m³/s; no annual volume is published.","APA/CADC annual report 2024/25"],["Barca de Alva — the historic Douro border gauge","decommissioned","Recorded EXTINTA in the SNIRH station register. So are Vila Velha de Ródão on the Tejo and Ponte Muge — the last of which CADC reports still cite as a live Convention control station. That contradiction is unresolved.","SNIRH station register"],["Reservoir evaporation","not published","No figure from APA, REN, EDP or EDIA. Academic estimates run 750–1,230 mm/yr.","—"],["Irrigation losses","not quantified","In APA's own Guadiana basin plan, the urban row of one indicator table carries a regulator, a year and a number. The agricultural row in the same table has no regulator, no baseline and no number — only a 2027 target.","APA PGRH RH7"],["Unlicensed abstraction","no statistics exist","APA's licensing page carries none; INE's compendium returns zero hits. The nearest evidence is a Gulbenkian farmer survey: 71% have no flow meter, 61% do not pay for water directly. That is a metering gap, not a count of illegal boreholes.","APA / INE / Fundação Calouste Gulbenkian (2020)"],["Saline intrusion — extent and volume","not published","Formally coded on exactly one groundwater body, Campina de Faro–Vale de Lobo, attributed verbatim to “as extrações existentes do setor agrícola e do golfe”. No chloride concentration, no extent, no affected volume published anywhere.","APA PGRH RH8"],["Algarve desalination — energy consumption","not published","Not in the contract announcement, the project hub page or the key-figures page. The ≈3.5 kWh/m³ and €0.51/m³ figures carried in earlier work are Porto Santo's, used as an analogy — they are not this plant's.","Águas do Algarve"],["Tariffs for public irrigation schemes other than Alqueva","not centrally published","DGADR's own 2024 Anuário defines “taxa de exploração (€/m³)” in its glossary and publishes no numeric value for any of the 33 schemes. Alqueva therefore cannot be shown to be typical, cheap or expensive.","DGADR"],["The 2024 sector balance","does not exist","The card reading “VOLUME DE ÁGUA CAPTADO POR SETOR (2024) — Fonte: APA” renders the PGRH 2018 dataset. On REA, “Fonte: APA, YYYY” is the year APA supplied the figure, never the data year.","REA / APA"],["Diário da República, programmatic access","closed","diariodarepublica.pt now returns the same 2,346-byte “JavaScript is required” shell to both curl and WebFetch. Verified with a known-positive that had been fetched successfully earlier the same day. Direct PDFs on files.diariodarepublica.pt still work if the exact path is known.","DRE"],["The 4,300–4,400 hm³ aquifer reserve","no primary source","The figure circulates. No document behind it was located.","—"]],"sources":[["i","CADC — Comissão para a Aplicação e Desenvolvimento da Convenção","Joint hydrometeorological reports and annual compliance reports, hydrological years 2005/06 to 2024/25; conclusions of the 1st–4th Conferences of the Parties","cadc-albufeira.eu / apambiente.pt"],["g","Diário da República","Convenção de Albufeira (RAR 66/1999); Protocolo de Revisão, DR 1.ª série n.º 222, 14-11-2008; Decreto-Lei 76/2016 (PNA); RCM 26-A/2024; RCM 80/2017; RCM 23/2024","files.diariodarepublica.pt"],["g","APA — Agência Portuguesa do Ambiente","PGRH 3.º ciclo 2022–2027, Parte 2 Volume A, all eight regions and the national summary (Quadro 4); hydrological-year reports 2023/24 and 2024/25; drought monitoring reports #30–#115; REA água","apambiente.pt / rea.apambiente.pt"],["g","IPMA","Climate normals 1971–2000, 1981–2010, 1991–2020; PDSI and SPI observatories; monthly and seasonal climate bulletins","ipma.pt / cs2.ipma.pt"],["g","ERSAR","RASARP 2025 (data 2024), Volume 1 and the per-entity annex — 214 retail operators","ersar.pt"],["g","EDIA","Relatório e Contas 2021 (carrying Despacho 3025/2017 in full); irrigation tariff simulator, 2026 campaign","edia.pt"],["g","Tribunal de Contas","Relatório de Auditoria n.º 3/2005 – 2.ª Secção, follow-up audit of EDIA / EFMA; index of all 1,577 audit reports 1999–2025","tcontas.pt"],["g","Governo de Portugal","“Água que Une — Estratégia Nacional para a Gestão da Água”, presentation of 9 March 2025","portugal.gov.pt"],["g","Águas do Algarve","Desalination contract and project pages; water reuse programme; July 2026 project update","aguasdoalgarve.pt"],["g","DGADR","Anuário dos Aproveitamentos Hidroagrícolas — Campanha de Rega 2024","sir.dgadr.gov.pt"],["g","MITECO (Spain)","BD-Embalses, reservoir database 1988–2026","miteco.gob.es"],["g","Confederaciones Hidrográficas del Duero, Tajo y Guadiana","Planes hidrológicos 2022–2027, memorias and demand annexes","chduero.es / chtajo.es / chguadiana.es"],["i","FAO AQUASTAT","Portugal water resources factsheet, ref. year 2022; Water Reports 23 (2003)","fao.org"],["i","Eurostat","env_wat_ltaa; env_wat_res; sdg_06_60 (WEI+)","ec.europa.eu/eurostat"],["i","OECD","DSD_WATER_RESOURCES, SDMX","sdmx.oecd.org"],["g","DGT","Carta Administrativa Oficial de Portugal 2025 — CC BY 4.0","geo2.dgterritorio.gov.pt"],["f","Fundação Calouste Gulbenkian","O uso da água em Portugal (2021) — farmer survey on metering and payment","gulbenkian.pt"],["f","Fundação Francisco Manuel dos Santos / RTP","“Onde está a água?”, documentary, June 2026 — the prompt for this study, and a source only for the claims tested here","ffms.pt / rtp.pt"]]}</script>
